{
  "meta": {
    "description": "Bangladesh government utility/infrastructure offices: WASA (Water Supply & Sewerage Authority), DESA's successor companies (DESCO/DPDC), and LGED (Local Government Engineering Department) district offices, with contact numbers and geolocation, sourced from Google Places data.",
    "important_notes": [
      "WASA is NOT a nationwide organization — it exists as an independent statutory body only in Dhaka, Chattogram, Khulna, and Rajshahi. Other cities' water supply is typically handled by the local City Corporation/Pourashava (municipality), not a separate WASA.",
      "DESA (Dhaka Electric Supply Authority) was abolished in 2008. Its assets and service area were split between two successor companies: DESCO (serves Mirpur & Gulshan areas of Dhaka) and DPDC (serves the rest of Dhaka city plus Narayanganj/Tongi). Entries under 'desa_successor_offices' represent these two companies, not a currently-operating 'DESA'.",
      "LGED has an office in every one of Bangladesh's 64 districts (plus HQ and divisional offices); one representative district office is listed per district here, not every upazila sub-office.",
      "Phone numbers are as publicly listed on Google Places; some offices had no listed number (shown as null)."
    ],
    "wasa_count": 7,
    "desa_successor_count": 3,
    "lged_count": 65
  },
